- ### Distributions
+ ### Distribuciones

- A random `Double` needs a shape, which a `Distribution` in scope supplies. Until the code says
- which kind of `Double` it means, one cannot be generated, which prevents the classic mistake of
- treating a uniform draw as though it were normal.
+ Un `Double` aleatorio necesita una forma, que proporciona una `Distribution` en el ámbito. Hasta que
+ el código diga a qué clase de `Double` se refiere, no se puede generar ninguno, lo que evita el error
+ clásico de tratar una extracción uniforme como si fuera normal.

= treating a uniform draw as though it were normal.
=
